WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:23.633 --> 00:00:25.133
[sighs]

00:00:32.533 --> 00:00:37.233
[geese honking]

00:00:37.233 --> 00:00:41.533
[goose honking]

00:00:41.833 --> 00:00:42.933
Day two.

00:00:43.299 --> 00:00:44.966
Ukrainian countryside.

00:00:47.166 --> 00:00:48.899
Started really nice.

00:00:49.299 --> 00:00:51.299
I don't know, 4:00 in the morning.

00:00:55.233 --> 00:00:57.733
And then the religious
music started playing.

00:00:58.700 --> 00:01:00.200
And I opened up the door

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:01.233
and looked into the living room

00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:05.400
and the family was
standing there praying.

00:01:06.366 --> 00:01:07.366
So

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.700
I jumped in.

00:01:09.466 --> 00:01:10.666
Closed my eyes

00:01:11.666 --> 00:01:13.566
and put my hands together.

00:01:14.233 --> 00:01:21.266
[praying]

00:01:21.266 --> 00:01:25.366
Your power, Lord, and glory unto the ages of ages.

00:01:25.366 --> 00:01:31.966
We thank You for choosing us,
delivering us from our sins, death and hell.

00:01:31.966 --> 00:01:38.000
Jesus, we thank You for enduring
until the end and walking to the cross

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.566
Jesus, You are our Lord.

00:01:40.599 --> 00:01:46.833
Lord, bless our guest, Peter.

00:01:46.833 --> 00:01:49.066
Bless him!

00:01:49.066 --> 00:01:52.299
Thank You, Lord!

00:01:52.299 --> 00:01:55.866
In the name of the Father, the Son and the Holy Spirit.

00:01:55.866 --> 00:01:57.299
Amen.

00:01:57.433 --> 00:01:59.866
Father, father! Geese! Geese!

00:01:59.866 --> 00:02:01.766
Geese, geese! Honk, honk, honk! [singing a song]

00:03:09.466 --> 00:03:11.066
You see...

00:03:11.800 --> 00:03:13.800
You don't have anything like this, do you?

00:03:16.599 --> 00:03:18.500
A guy came by today.

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.733
A neighbor

00:03:19.733 --> 00:03:21.766
and he had this

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:25.066
little metal thing in his hand

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:28.266
and it was just sort of spinning around.

00:03:28.599 --> 00:03:29.599
And

00:03:30.066 --> 00:03:32.800
when it would get the right point

00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:35.066
he would sort of stop.

00:03:35.300 --> 00:03:39.933
And what they were looking to
do is find where to dig the well.

00:03:41.433 --> 00:03:42.433
We have to

00:03:43.000 --> 00:03:44.966
use buckets in the bath tub

00:03:44.966 --> 00:03:46.466
and there's not drain in the bath tub.

00:03:46.466 --> 00:03:49.366
So we have to bucket
in the bath tub and then

00:03:50.166 --> 00:03:51.699
extract the water.

00:03:52.666 --> 00:03:56.366
[water splashing]

00:04:05.666 --> 00:04:06.599
It's like...

00:04:06.800 --> 00:04:09.966
we've been carrying the water for 4 years.

00:04:10.699 --> 00:04:12.699
4 years.

00:04:13.699 --> 00:04:17.133
But we got lucky that our neighbours don't live here.

00:04:17.199 --> 00:04:19.199
If they had lived,

00:04:19.733 --> 00:04:21.733
then I don't know...

00:04:21.800 --> 00:04:23.800
We'd have had to buy it then.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:29.333
Family is fantastic.

00:04:29.333 --> 00:04:31.199
Wonderful, beautiful people.

00:04:31.266 --> 00:04:32.433
Beautiful, beautiful people.

00:04:32.433 --> 00:04:32.933
Really cool.

00:04:32.933 --> 00:04:34.100
Who is this?

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:35.333
That's a pancake.

00:04:40.500 --> 00:04:41.833
And what are you doing?

00:04:41.899 --> 00:04:43.699
And then Valeriy sat me down

00:04:44.366 --> 00:04:45.966
next to the computer

00:04:46.399 --> 00:04:47.500
and he played this video

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.199
or a couple videos of

00:04:49.566 --> 00:04:51.266
blown out apartments.

00:04:52.566 --> 00:04:54.699
And then he told me that was

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.133
The building

00:04:56.333 --> 00:04:57.833
that they lived in.

00:04:58.399 --> 00:04:59.233
Your house?

00:04:59.233 --> 00:04:59.933
Yes.

00:04:59.933 --> 00:05:01.066
My father is there.

00:05:01.066 --> 00:05:02.766
My father is there now.

00:05:04.233 --> 00:05:04.966
Here it is.

00:05:06.133 --> 00:05:08.666
Today I was studying with Alisa.

00:05:10.399 --> 00:05:12.033
Babóoshka [Grandmother]

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:13.166
Grandmother, right.

00:05:13.166 --> 00:05:16.100
Not “babóoshka”, no. Bа́booshka.

00:05:16.100 --> 00:05:17.833
Bа́booshka.

00:05:17.833 --> 00:05:18.766
Thank you.

00:05:18.800 --> 00:05:21.666
She was correcting my
pronunciation in Russian.

00:05:21.766 --> 00:05:23.866
He was listening to “operU” [wrong Russian pronunciation] [English: opera].

00:05:23.866 --> 00:05:25.199
He was istening to “operU”?

00:05:25.199 --> 00:05:27.300
Listening to “operU”.

00:05:27.300 --> 00:05:28.266
Listening…

00:05:28.266 --> 00:05:29.199
To “operU”.

00:05:29.199 --> 00:05:29.766
“Operu”, yes?

00:05:29.766 --> 00:05:30.266
Yes.

00:05:30.266 --> 00:05:31.199
Listening to “operU”.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:31.699
Yes.

00:05:31.699 --> 00:05:33.899
He was listening to “Operu”.

00:05:34.300 --> 00:05:35.466
Yes.

00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:37.100
Right.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.500
She's such a little ray of sunshine.

00:05:40.500 --> 00:05:43.899
Such a beautiful human being.

00:05:45.866 --> 00:05:48.300
And then Mark came up.

00:05:48.500 --> 00:05:49.699
The little guy.

00:05:50.199 --> 00:05:53.166
He's only two but he's got a really

00:05:53.733 --> 00:05:55.266
bubbly personality.

00:05:55.266 --> 00:05:58.100
And Max, Max really opened up today.

00:05:58.433 --> 00:05:59.633
He got behind the camera a little.

00:05:59.633 --> 00:06:02.466
Shooting some stuff and I
want to get him on this project.

00:06:02.466 --> 00:06:04.833
To actually shoot some footage

00:06:04.833 --> 00:06:07.100
because he seems super interested.

00:06:08.866 --> 00:06:10.366
You’re my friend.

00:06:11.100 --> 00:06:13.100
You’re my friend too.

00:06:19.533 --> 00:06:21.699
First impressions of Valeriy

00:06:21.699 --> 00:06:24.166
are he's got this bad boy look to him

00:06:24.166 --> 00:06:25.433
with the tattoos

00:06:25.866 --> 00:06:28.533
but it takes very little time around him

00:06:28.833 --> 00:06:30.600
to feel the genuine

00:06:31.033 --> 00:06:34.033
and warm side of this man.

00:06:39.566 --> 00:06:40.566
[laughter]

00:06:40.733 --> 00:06:43.833
Well, that's when the frog
hunting process started.

00:06:43.833 --> 00:06:44.866
So we walked

00:06:45.399 --> 00:06:46.899
down this dirt road

00:06:48.066 --> 00:06:50.066
on this pathway down to the river

00:06:50.066 --> 00:06:51.100
and it's a real

00:06:51.633 --> 00:06:53.000
narrow river.

00:06:53.833 --> 00:06:55.266
Valeriy was hilarious.

00:06:55.266 --> 00:06:56.833
I mean he was out there like a hunter.

00:06:56.833 --> 00:06:58.833
Like a true primitive man.

00:06:58.833 --> 00:07:03.366
He had his little stick and his net

00:07:04.100 --> 00:07:06.933
and he assumed the position

00:07:07.266 --> 00:07:09.199
of this hunter-gatherer guy

00:07:09.199 --> 00:07:10.333
and he's good.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.500
He got up

00:07:12.166 --> 00:07:13.233
and

00:07:13.233 --> 00:07:14.800
killed these frogs and then

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:16.866
smacked them on the rocks.

00:07:23.133 --> 00:07:25.933
And yeah, it can be looked at as cruel but

00:07:26.933 --> 00:07:28.633
I don't know, we ate the food

00:07:29.533 --> 00:07:31.800
within an hour afterwards.

00:07:33.033 --> 00:07:34.300
Super.

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:48.199
First time a frog.

00:07:53.466 --> 00:07:54.266
Yes.

00:07:55.133 --> 00:07:56.333
Tasty.

00:07:59.333 --> 00:08:01.066
And that was my first time

00:08:01.366 --> 00:08:02.633
having frog legs

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:04.133
and they were amazing.

00:08:04.133 --> 00:08:05.666
Really exceptional.

00:08:05.899 --> 00:08:08.500
And then we’ll catch the lizards.

00:08:08.766 --> 00:08:09.666
The lizards?

00:08:09.666 --> 00:08:10.166
The lizards.

00:08:10.166 --> 00:08:11.466
Yes, yes, yes.

00:08:17.800 --> 00:08:19.800
Well done!

00:08:22.500 --> 00:08:23.866
Now dad is going to poison them.

00:08:28.233 --> 00:08:29.233
[laughter]

00:08:42.266 --> 00:08:43.500
Practice.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:45.466
You have to practice.

00:08:47.700 --> 00:08:48.700
He's

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:50.233
got an open heart.

00:08:50.233 --> 00:08:52.533
He's a very loving father.

00:08:55.600 --> 00:09:01.166
And you can tell that his family
is absolutely everything to him.

00:09:09.799 --> 00:09:11.266
It’s wounded.

00:09:14.700 --> 00:09:16.299
Peter, I was thinking…

00:09:16.399 --> 00:09:18.600
maybe I should leave everything.

00:09:18.600 --> 00:09:21.633
Anyways, we don’t have much to lose

00:09:22.000 --> 00:09:25.766
and go live in the woods

00:09:25.766 --> 00:09:31.066
where there’s no money, no electricity,
no Internet, no computers

00:09:31.066 --> 00:09:32.866
absolutely nothing.

00:09:32.866 --> 00:09:34.799
But from the different perspective

00:09:34.799 --> 00:09:37.766
what will happen to the kids, what about the civilization?

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.799
How will they grow up in a place where there’s nothing?

00:09:42.733 --> 00:09:44.733
Will they thank us afterwards?

00:09:45.299 --> 00:09:48.166
Oh, and then I walked
in the living room

00:09:48.166 --> 00:09:51.866
and Valeriy was getting ready for a tattoo.

00:09:52.366 --> 00:09:53.966
[tattoo gun buzzing]

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.166
So there's this kid in here that...

00:10:01.166 --> 00:10:04.600
What did it say?
It said something on his fists like...

00:10:04.600 --> 00:10:06.733
Like f*ck off or something like that.

00:10:06.733 --> 00:10:07.766
I forget.

00:10:07.766 --> 00:10:08.766
And...

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.500
He worked on Valeriy for awhile.

00:10:12.766 --> 00:10:14.766
Let me tell you…

00:10:14.766 --> 00:10:19.166
Back when I was in the army,
I made a tattoo with an image of death

00:10:19.600 --> 00:10:21.899
When I learned about the Bible

00:10:21.899 --> 00:10:25.466
it’s written there that if
a person makes the tattoo

00:10:25.466 --> 00:10:30.600
with the image of a skull or death,
it’s called as the signet of the devil.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:33.100
And it means that you go to hell immediately.

00:10:33.466 --> 00:10:36.600
There’s even no chance to get to the court of God.

00:10:37.366 --> 00:10:39.966
That’s why I decided to cover my tattoo

00:10:39.966 --> 00:10:43.000
with the image of God, Jesus Christ.

00:10:48.566 --> 00:10:50.100
During the prayer session

00:10:50.100 --> 00:10:51.100
this morning

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:52.700
a new guy walked in.

00:10:53.066 --> 00:10:54.766
And his name is Oleg.

00:10:55.566 --> 00:10:58.433
And he is the well digger.

00:11:00.200 --> 00:11:02.066
when they said they were gonna dig a well

00:11:02.066 --> 00:11:03.600
I was thinking, you know

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:06.100
bring a machine in and

00:11:06.100 --> 00:11:07.366
drill out a well.

00:11:07.366 --> 00:11:10.033
I had no idea they were talking about...

00:11:10.200 --> 00:11:13.966
Today we will be digging a well.

00:11:14.366 --> 00:11:16.100
Shovel by shovel

00:11:16.100 --> 00:11:18.066
digging this well until

00:11:18.566 --> 00:11:20.233
you actually hit water.

00:11:22.500 --> 00:11:24.033
Teacher, is it good?

00:11:27.600 --> 00:11:28.500
What?

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:34.600
Mark!

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:35.866
Come here!

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:43.299
Poo poo.

00:11:43.299 --> 00:11:44.733
[toy gun]

00:11:54.299 --> 00:11:55.200
What is that?

00:11:55.200 --> 00:11:55.966
“Aria” [music band]

00:11:56.200 --> 00:11:57.000
“Aria”.

00:11:58.266 --> 00:11:59.233
Is it rock?

00:11:59.566 --> 00:12:00.233
Yes.

00:12:00.366 --> 00:12:01.666
Or metal?

00:12:02.166 --> 00:12:03.366
Rock.

00:12:05.966 --> 00:12:07.399
“I love…” [singing the song].

00:12:14.433 --> 00:12:15.433
Nice guy.

00:12:15.733 --> 00:12:16.733
Big smile.

00:12:17.566 --> 00:12:20.433
Real soft, gentle, humble guy.

00:12:20.566 --> 00:12:22.100
I enjoyed digging with him today

00:12:22.100 --> 00:12:24.233
even though I have to say he did

00:12:24.600 --> 00:12:25.966
most of the work.

00:12:36.200 --> 00:12:37.600
Alisa, what are you doing?

00:12:37.600 --> 00:12:38.799
Digging.

00:12:39.899 --> 00:12:41.833
Helping my parents.

00:12:47.066 --> 00:12:49.066
Take a photo of us from the bottom.

00:12:49.066 --> 00:12:51.433
And we will stand like this here.

00:13:03.333 --> 00:13:04.766
Today was...

00:13:06.600 --> 00:13:08.266
A very interesting day.

00:13:09.066 --> 00:13:12.633
And what is it, my third day
out here in the countryside?

00:13:13.766 --> 00:13:16.266
Yeah, feels like I've
been here much longer.

00:13:17.966 --> 00:13:19.966
Starting to feel this place.

00:13:21.733 --> 00:13:24.200
It hasn't taken me long to really

00:13:24.666 --> 00:13:26.766
warm up to Volare

00:13:27.666 --> 00:13:29.166
and we do simple things.

00:13:29.166 --> 00:13:30.166
We go to

00:13:31.066 --> 00:13:32.933
a berry tree and eat berries together

00:13:32.933 --> 00:13:34.733
or walk to a lake.

00:13:41.200 --> 00:13:42.200
Конопля?

00:13:42.200 --> 00:13:43.133
Cannibus.

00:13:43.133 --> 00:13:43.799
Cannibus.

00:13:43.799 --> 00:13:44.399
Yes.

00:13:44.600 --> 00:13:45.600
Laugh a lot.

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.466
I mean I don't understand
everything he's saying

00:13:48.466 --> 00:13:50.466
probably more like 40%.

00:13:51.899 --> 00:13:53.600
But it really doesn't matter.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:54.333
You like it?

00:13:54.533 --> 00:13:54.899
Me?

00:13:54.899 --> 00:13:55.399
Yes.

00:13:56.200 --> 00:13:59.700
I have smoked so much of it.

00:13:59.799 --> 00:14:01.466
And now, I don’t do it anymore.

00:14:02.399 --> 00:14:03.700
Natural.

00:14:31.899 --> 00:14:35.000
Yeah, it's just this exotic place.

00:14:35.266 --> 00:14:38.066
Not exotic like the tropics of

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:40.799
Southeast Asia.

00:14:41.666 --> 00:14:44.266
But exotic in the
sense that it's totally...

00:14:44.266 --> 00:14:46.466
It's totally a different reality here.

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:59.066
-To-ma-to.
-Tomato.

00:14:59.066 --> 00:15:02.533
-Be-ans. 
-Beans.

00:15:03.399 --> 00:15:05.066
Cu-cum-ber.

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.200
-Cucumber. 
- Cucumber.

00:15:09.266 --> 00:15:10.266
It feels...

00:15:10.266 --> 00:15:11.966
This fish out of water...

00:15:15.133 --> 00:15:18.700
Olya, who is my friend and is also
doing the translation for this video

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:19.533
She gave this to me.

00:15:19.533 --> 00:15:22.733
I definitely feel like this here.

00:15:23.299 --> 00:15:24.899
Things got picked up.

00:15:32.333 --> 00:15:35.200
Don’t cut it too short. Cut it here. Over here.

00:15:37.733 --> 00:15:39.000
Well

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:40.666
that was about it today.

00:15:41.433 --> 00:15:43.100
It's just pure simplicity.

00:15:43.100 --> 00:15:44.100
Pure beauty.

00:15:45.533 --> 00:15:47.566
Pure connectivity between the family...

00:15:47.566 --> 00:15:50.000
Between the family and nature.

00:15:53.700 --> 00:15:55.966
Cool, the field…

00:15:59.466 --> 00:16:01.066
Tomorrow is another adventure.

00:16:01.066 --> 00:16:02.000
I don't know where we're going.

00:16:02.000 --> 00:16:04.266
We're going somewhere at 8:30
and I couldn't really understand

00:16:04.266 --> 00:16:05.933
what they were saying.

00:16:06.033 --> 00:16:07.466
That's sort of my story here.

00:16:07.466 --> 00:16:10.399
I can't really understand
much of what's going on.

00:16:10.399 --> 00:16:11.399
So

00:16:11.633 --> 00:16:13.066
that's it for now.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.200
Until tomorrow.

